  "id": "philadelphia",
  "intro": "Philadelphia has the busiest stretch of river in the northeast that nobody thinks about. The Delaware carries more tanker and container traffic than the Hudson, the refineries and terminals run from the city down past Wilmington, and the pilots working it are on VHF around the clock. The airport sits directly on the river, so approach traffic and ship traffic are audible from the same spot. Inland, this is the densest part of the Northeast Corridor, with passenger and freight rail on every side.",
  "introz": "费城拥有美国东北部最繁忙、却最少被提起的一段河道。特拉华河上的油轮和集装箱船流量超过哈德逊河，炼油厂和码头从市区一路延伸到威尔明顿以南，引航员昼夜都在 VHF 上工作。机场就在河边，所以在同一个位置能同时听到进近通话和船舶通话。往内陆，这里是东北走廊最密集的一段，四面都是客运和货运铁路。",
